            "LineonCheckerTests.test_default_receipt_and_sections_have_unique_exact_statuses"
          ],
          "requirement_id": "TFQM-LINEON-REVIEW-CHECK-TFQ-1219-FSP-HINGE-LINEON-SIGN-CLAIM-3"
        },
        {
          "requirement": "Require exact bool flags and exact rational traces; projection is the literal identity/square toy rule, defect mass is a sign indicator and routing is a closed two-label truth table. Validate both flags before branch short circuit.",
          "symbols": [
            "_flag",
            "evaluate_foliated_projected_trace",
            "compute_defect_mass_phi1",
            "evaluate_terminal_routing"
          ],
          "tests": [
            "LineonCheckerTests.test_projection_mass_and_routing_are_literal_toy_rules",
            "LineonCheckerTests.test_trace_and_flag_refusals_precede_branching"
          ],
          "requirement_id": "TFQM-LINEON-REVIEW-CHECK-TFQ-1219-FSP-HINGE-LINEON-SIGN-CLAIM-4"
        },
        {
          "requirement": "Admit a scalar exact trace in [-2,2]; return exact symbolic acos(trace/2), simplifying only five integral traces and suppressing general symbolic evaluation. The result alone does not certify any matrix domain.",
